// Layout control is offered on types with a STRUCT, which an enum is not: a payload-less one lowers to an
// integer and a tagged one to a tag plus a per-variant union — and a `packed` on that outer struct would
// not reach the inner payload structs, so the attribute would half work. One rejection is the honest
// answer. What an enum CAN state about its layout is its tag width, `type enum E : IntType`.
//
// This used to compile CLEAN with the attribute silently dropped: the enum collect loop skipped every
// attribute name it did not recognize, and there was no catch-all.
@packed
type enum Color : uint8 { Red, Green, Blue }

fn int32 main() { return cast<int32>(Color::Blue); }
